10	// Regression tests for the pinned circuit version on a committed job record.
11	// The "version" a job writes is the sole authority for which frozen circuit —
12	// and thereby which trusted setup and compiled artifact — the job belongs to.
13	// Any spelling the ordinary read would fill Version from names that one
14	// field: the canonical "version", an ASCII letter-case variant, a JSON-escaped
15	// spelling, or the Unicode-folded long-s "verſion" (U+017F). Two such
16	// spellings on one record make the version a function of key order
17	// (encoding/json keeps the last value) and are refused as data corruption —
18	// equal or differing values, both legal, and even with unrelated fields
19	// interleaved. A long-s spelling standing alone is still the single version
20	// field and keeps reading as it does today.
